# Rust / Cargo
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak
# Shared Cargo build directories. Nothing in this repo configures them — a
# machine-level `~/.cargo/config.toml` may point `build.target-dir` here so
# that every git worktree reuses one set of dependency artifacts instead of
# keeping its own multi-GB `src-tauri/target/`. Harmless on machines that do
# not set it; ignored so the (large, untracked) directories can never be staged
# by a `git add -A` on machines that do. The wildcard also covers the
# per-worktree variants (`.cargo-target-<worktree>/`) that such a config
# produces — one of those reached a clone's object store via `git add -A`,
# leaving ~900 MB of unreachable build artifacts behind.
/.cargo-target*/

# Tauri
/src-tauri/target/
/src-tauri/Cargo.lock.bak
/src-tauri/gen/
.tauri/

